================================================================
sw-ibm1130-forth historical/forth68/  -- attribution + provenance
================================================================

This directory contains a translation of Charles H. Moore's
1968 FORTH for the IBM 1130, redistributed under the
public-posting permission Moore granted in May 2020.

Original work
-------------
    "FORTH" -- the first implementation of the Forth language.
    Author : Charles H. Moore.
    Year   : 1968.
    Place  : Mohasco Industries, Amsterdam, NY.
    Target : IBM 1130 with 2250 graphic display.
    Form   : 645-line IBM 1130 assembly source ("FORTH68asm.txt"
             in the upstream copy) plus a 235-line FORTH-level
             listing dumped from the 1130 disk
             ("FORTH68lst.txt"), originally created as a deck of
             punched cards.

Redistribution permission
-------------------------
    Charles H. Moore granted permission for public posting of
    the recovered source in May 2020. The publicly-available
    copy at https://github.com/monsonite/1968-FORTH is hosted
    under that permission. This directory's redistribution
    operates under the same permission, with attribution to
    Moore (the original author) and to monsonite/1968-FORTH (the
    upstream copy we translated from).

Upstream copy translated from
-----------------------------
    Repository : https://github.com/monsonite/1968-FORTH
    Revision   : (recorded in TRANSLATION-LOG.md when this
                  directory is populated by the forth-on-1130
                  saga)

Translation
-----------
    Translator : Michael A Wright, 2026.
    Scope      : syntactic retargeting (column layout, directive
                 names, EBCDIC literal handling, BSC mask
                 encoding) so the source compiles under our
                 sw-ibm1130-asm and runs under our
                 sw-ibm1130-emulator. Algorithm, primitive set,
                 and identifier choices are unchanged from
                 Moore's 1968 source.
    Log        : every transformation is documented in
                 TRANSLATION-LOG.md.

If Moore or his estate ever objects to this redistribution, we
will retire this directory and revert to the reference-only
model documented in docs/references.md.

